This file lists the third-party models, runtimes and components that Parlora
Tutor depends on, adapts or recommends. Each one keeps its own licence or
terms, which apply to that component and are not changed by Parlora Tutor's
licence. Components marked "planned" arrive with the voice pipeline (Phase 1)
and are not yet installed by this repository. Components marked "bench" are
installed only by the optional `bench` dependency group and the local `bench`
image used by the component benchmarks (scripts/bench); `just setup` and the
server's runtime image do not install them.

Model weights are never stored in this repository; they are downloaded by the
user from their original source and are subject to that source's terms.


Speech recognition
------------------

Whisper (OpenAI) — model weights and reference code — MIT License. Planned.
  https://github.com/openai/whisper

faster-whisper (SYSTRAN) and CTranslate2 (OpenNMT) — MIT License. Bench;
  planned for the voice pipeline.
  https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper

NVIDIA CUDA libraries — nvidia-cublas-cu12, nvidia-cudnn-cu12 and
  nvidia-cuda-nvrtc-cu12 — NVIDIA proprietary licences (NVIDIA Software License
  Agreement and the CUDA Toolkit End User License Agreement). Bench. The CUDA
  user-space libraries that CTranslate2 loads on the GPU, installed as pip
  wheels from PyPI on the user's machine. They are not redistributed: the
  repository does not contain them and Parlora Tutor does not publish container
  images. The dependency licence check allows them as a reviewed exception
  (docs/adr/0002-server-gpu-runtime-in-docker.md).
  https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/


Speech synthesis
----------------

Kokoro-82M (hexgrad) — model weights — Apache License 2.0. Planned.
  https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M

misaki (hexgrad) — grapheme-to-phoneme library — Apache License 2.0. Bench;
  planned for the voice pipeline. Used without extras. Parlora Tutor also
  adapts misaki's table that maps espeak-ng IPA phonemes to Kokoro phonemes;
  that code is used under the Apache License 2.0 with attribution.
  https://github.com/hexgrad/misaki

kokoro-onnx (thewh1teagle) — MIT License. Bench; planned for the voice
  pipeline. Parlora Tutor does not install this package (it pulls in GPL
  code); it adapts parts of its ONNX runner under the MIT License, with
  attribution.
  https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx

espeak-ng — GNU General Public License v3.0 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later).
  Planned. Used only as a separate executable for words missing from the
  pronunciation dictionary (out-of-vocabulary words): Parlora Tutor starts the
  `espeak-ng` program as a separate process, passes it one word and reads back
  the phonemes. No espeak-ng code is linked, imported or contained in this
  repository. The server image's local `bench` target installs the Debian
  `espeak-ng` package when the user builds it; the runtime image does not, and
  Parlora Tutor does not publish container images. Any
  distributed image that contains espeak-ng must meet the GPL-3.0 terms for that
  component. See docs/adr/0004-kokoro-g2p-and-gpl-boundary.md.
  https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng

spaCy and the en_core_web_sm model (Explosion) — MIT License. Bench; planned
  for the voice pipeline.
  https://github.com/explosion/spaCy

onnxruntime (Microsoft) — MIT License. Bench; planned for the voice pipeline.
  Runs the Kokoro ONNX model on the CPU.
  https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime


