LGPL Python packages
--------------------

These packages are used unmodified through normal Python imports, each
reviewed and listed as an exception in the dependency licence check
(docs/adr/0004-kokoro-g2p-and-gpl-boundary.md,
docs/adr/0005-python-dependency-policy-enforcement.md):

soxr (python-soxr) — GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 or later
  (LGPL-2.1-or-later). Pulled in by Pipecat. Planned.
  https://github.com/dofuuz/python-soxr

num2words — GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 (LGPL-2.1). Pulled in by
  misaki's English G2P. Bench; planned for the voice pipeline.
  https://github.com/savoirfairelinux/num2words


Other dependencies
------------------

The remaining Python and JavaScript dependencies are installed from the
lockfiles (uv.lock, pnpm-lock.yaml) under permissive licences (MIT, BSD,
Apache-2.0, ISC, PSF) or MPL-2.0. CI rejects GPL and AGPL dependencies and any
dependency whose licence cannot be identified.
